"""Publish the Oracle Always Free eligibility guide; no account or live entitlement assumptions."""
from linode_article import publish_document
from hetzner_article import table

CHECKED = '2026-11-13T07:11:23.593871+00:00'
RESOURCES = 'https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm'
OVERVIEW = 'https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier.htm'
FAQ = 'https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/faq/'
PRICES = 'https://www.oracle.com/cloud/price-list/'

def body():
    result = '''<h1>Oracle Cloud free tier: $0 starting cost within verified limits</h1>
<p><strong>Eligible Always Free infrastructure starts at $0, with no time limit on the allowance itself.</strong> That is a conditional starting cost, not an unlimited server: the current technical documentation lists up to two AMD Micro VMs and an A1 allowance of 1,500 OCPU-hours and 9,000 GB-hours per month, with 200 GB of combined boot/block storage and 10 TB of monthly outbound data. Your home region, shape, capacity and account limits must qualify. Idle VMs may be reclaimed. <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Official Always Free Resources → introduction, Compute, Block Volume and Outbound Data Transfer</a>.</p>
<h2>The free-resource budget, before you create a VM</h2>
<p>This guide focuses on compute, storage and network resources for a small server. It is not a complete catalog of Oracle's free database and platform services. The values below are the current technical documentation's published values, not an assertion about an existing account's grandfathered limits.</p>'''
    result += table(['Resource','Published Always Free amount','Official section and condition'],[
        ['AMD compute','Up to 2 × VM.Standard.E2.1.Micro; each 1/8 OCPU and 1 GB RAM','Compute → Available Shapes and Details; home region'],
        ['Arm compute','VM.Standard.A1.Flex: 1,500 OCPU-hours/month and 9,000 GB-hours/month','Compute → Available Shapes; described as 2 OCPUs and 12 GB total'],
        ['Boot + block volumes','200 GB total, combined','Block Volume; home region'],
        ['Volume backups','5 total, boot and block combined','Block Volume → Details'],
        ['Object storage, Always Free-only account','20 GB combined across Standard, Infrequent Access and Archive; 50,000 API requests/month','Object and Archive Storage → expired-trial / Always Free-only case'],
        ['Outbound transfer','10 TB/month','Additional Services → Outbound Data Transfer'],
    ],'Oracle free resource budget')
    result += '''<p>Data from <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Oracle official Always Free Resources</a>, named sections in the final column. Checked 2026-11-13 07:11 UTC. Always Free eligibility must be checked in the Console; a published allowance is not a reservation of physical capacity. Trial and paid-account object-storage allocations differ, so the object-storage row is deliberately limited to the Always Free-only case.</p>
<h2>Do the A1 hours fit your month?</h2>
<section data-authored-calculation="hours"><p><strong>Our assumption:</strong> one A1 VM is retained for every hour of a 31-day month, with 2 OCPUs and 12 GB RAM; no other A1 instances consume the allowance. Hours = 31 × 24 = 744. CPU usage = 2 × 744 = 1,488 OCPU-hours; memory usage = 12 × 744 = 8,928 GB-hours. Against the <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Compute → Available Shapes limits of 1,500 and 9,000</a>, the remaining budgets are 1,500 − 1,488 = 12 OCPU-hours and 9,000 − 8,928 = 72 GB-hours. This is a resource-budget calculation, not measured use or a guarantee that the VM is available.</p>
<p><strong>Our assumption:</strong> compare a proposed 4-OCPU, 24-GB configuration for the same 744 hours. It needs 4 × 744 = 2,976 OCPU-hours and 24 × 744 = 17,856 GB-hours. Relative to the current technical-document limits, the excess is max(0, 2,976 − 1,500) = 1,476 OCPU-hours and max(0, 17,856 − 9,000) = 8,856 GB-hours. Those are hypothetical resource quantities, not a promise a free-only account can provision that configuration.</p>
<p>Do not turn the excess into a dollar bill using an old tutorial. The current public <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/price-list/">OCI Price List → Ampere A1 OCPU and Memory rows</a> did not yield readable unit-price values in this check, and its pricing markers differ from the current technical-document allowance. The account-specific threshold and a reconciled current paid quote are <strong>Not obtained</strong>; the selected account's entitlement and current A1 paid price are needed. We therefore publish no paid A1 total.</p></section>
<h2>Boot disks spend the same storage allowance</h2>
<section data-authored-calculation="storage"><p><strong>Our assumption:</strong> use one eligible AMD VM and one eligible A1 VM, each with the documented default 50 GB boot volume, plus a 100 GB data volume in the home region. Allocated capacity = 2 × <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">50 GB</a> + 100 GB = 200 GB; remaining capacity = <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">200 GB</a> − 200 GB = 0 GB. An additional 50 GB volume would take the allocation to 250 GB, or 50 GB above that shared budget. It does not get a new free pool because it is a separate disk.</p>
<p>Inputs of 200 GB and default 50 GB come from <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Block Volume → opening paragraph and Details</a>. The data-volume sizes and selected combination are our assumptions. The same document's earlier Compute example refers to a 47 GB minimum, while Block Volume describes a 50 GB default/minimum; this scenario explicitly uses the 50 GB default, not the inconsistent minimum. The selected image's actual minimum is <strong>Not obtained</strong>; check its create-instance form.</p>
<p>Backup count is another limit: our assumption of 3 boot-volume backups plus 2 data-volume backups uses 3 + 2 = <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">5 free backups</a>. A sixth Always Free backup is not an automatic paid add-on: <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Block Volume → final backup-limit paragraph</a> says creating it fails until an existing backup is deleted. A paid-account backup configuration requires its own quote.</p></section>
<h2>Three events that do different things to your bill</h2>'''
    result += table(['Event','Account state / outcome','What to verify'],[
        ['Usage exceeds an allowance','A paid account can incur charges above the free limits; trial usage can consume remaining trial credit','Resource eligibility, meter and current paid unit price'],
        ['You voluntarily upgrade the account','Always Free resources remain free within their limits; paid resource usage can be billed','Review retained resources and quotas before upgrading'],
        ['The trial expires or credit runs out','Without a paid upgrade, eligible Always Free resources remain; paid trial resources are reclaimed','Expiry is not itself consent to paid billing; reduce trial-only resources before the deadline'],
    ],'Trial expiry versus paid usage')
    result += '''<p>Data from <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier.htm">Oracle official Free Tier → Free Trial, When Your Trial Period Ends and Upgrading to a Paid Account</a>; <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Always Free Resources → Compute, capacity note</a>; <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/faq/">Free Tier FAQ → larger resources and upgrade questions</a>. Checked 2026-11-13 07:11 UTC. The trial credit is US$300 for up to 30 days, ending earlier if exhausted. These rules do not quote a complete VM bill.</p>
<p>Oracle's <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier.htm">When Your Trial Period Ends, A1 note</a> says an over-limit A1 allocation is disabled and then deleted after 30 days unless the account is upgraded. It tells free users to reduce their combined A1 allocation to no more than 2 OCPUs and 12 GB before the trial ends. Do not assume that leaving the larger trial shape in place preserves the free shape automatically.</p>
<p><strong>Our assumption:</strong> an Always Free-only transition leaves 21 GB in Object Storage. The documented combined limit is <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">20 GB</a>, so 21 − 20 = 1 GB is over the limit. The consequence in <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Object and Archive Storage → Important, final paragraph</a> is deletion of all objects if the account is over the limit when the trial ends, not just the excess 1 GB. This scenario is a data-loss check, not a storage invoice.</p>
<h2>Idle reclamation: test the conditions together</h2>
<p>Oracle may reclaim an idle Always Free compute instance when all applicable tests hold over a 7-day period: 95th-percentile CPU utilization below 20%, network utilization below 20%, and, for A1 only, memory utilization below 20%. These are the tests in <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Always Free Resources → Compute → Idle Compute Instances</a>. The CPU statistic is not simply the average CPU figure.</p>'''
    result += table(['A1 scenario: our assumptions over the full test window','CPU p95','Network','Memory','All three stated tests hold?'],[
        ['A','19%','19%','19%','Yes: 19 < 20 in all three tests; may be reclaimed'],
        ['B','21%','19%','19%','No: CPU is not below 20%'],
        ['C','19%','19%','21%','No: A1 memory is not below 20%'],
    ],'Idle-condition worked examples')
    result += '''<p>Policy data from <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Oracle official Always Free Resources → Idle Compute Instances</a>. Checked 2026-11-13 07:11 UTC. The 19% and 21% readings are our assumptions, not observed metrics. Formula for A1: idle-test = (CPU p95 &lt; 20%) AND (network &lt; 20%) AND (memory &lt; 20%); the memory test does not apply to the AMD Micro shape.</p>
<p>“May be reclaimed” is not a guaranteed deletion schedule, and failing this test is not a guarantee of continued service under every account policy. The exact notice period, recovery procedure and whether a particular reclaimed VM's boot volume is retained are <strong>Not obtained</strong>; an explicit current compute-reclamation policy or Oracle confirmation is needed. Keep an independent recovery copy rather than treating free capacity as reserved infrastructure. Separately, the <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/faq/">FAQ → Who is eligible?</a> says accounts idle for 30 days or more may be considered abandoned and suspended or terminated. That is an account rule, not the same 7-day VM test.</p>
<h2>Oracle Cloud pricing after the free boundary</h2>'''
    result += table(['Billable input needed','Unit / scope to request','Current rate obtained'],[
        ['A1 compute and memory','USD per OCPU-hour and per GB-hour; reconcile account allowance first','Not obtained: readable current price and account threshold needed'],
        ['Additional block storage and performance','Storage GB-month plus selected performance tier / VPU charges','Not obtained: selected volume size, performance and current quote needed'],
        ['Outbound transfer beyond the free amount','Selected origin/destination zone and billable GB beyond allowance','Not obtained: route and current official rate needed'],
        ['Paid backup / object storage','Selected storage tier, retained GB and operations','Not obtained: tier, quantities and current official quote needed'],
    ],'Paid inputs not quoted')
    result += '''<p>Data checked against <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/price-list/">Oracle official OCI Price List → Compute, Networking and Storage tables</a>. Checked 2026-11-13 07:11 UTC. Numeric unit-price cells were not obtained in the public page read. No third-party or historical price has been substituted. For a paid account the resource-cost expression is max(0, CPU-hours − applicable free CPU-hours) × CPU rate + max(0, GB-hours − applicable free GB-hours) × memory rate + separately priced storage/network/other services. Every missing input must be resolved before that expression becomes a quote.</p>
<h2>Eligibility, regions and account count</h2>
<p>The documented free compute shapes are VM.Standard.E2.1.Micro and VM.Standard.A1.Flex; this guide makes no free claim for other shapes or a non-eligible image. Compute and free block volumes must be in the tenancy's home region. The A1 availability-domain exception names South Korea North (Chuncheon). The <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier.htm">Free Tier overview</a> excludes US Government Cloud regions. A complete current region-by-shape stock matrix is <strong>Not obtained</strong>; current Console capacity is needed. An out-of-host-capacity error means capacity is unavailable, not that another account is allowed.</p>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Always Free Resources → Compute → Available Shapes and capacity note; Block Volume → Important</a>. The <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/faq/">official FAQ → Who is eligible for Oracle Cloud Free Tier?</a> permits one Free Trial or Always Free account per person and prohibits attempts to create multiple free accounts. We do not suggest creating extra accounts to bypass capacity limits.</p>
<h2>Who this fits, and what was not obtained</h2>
<p>This is useful for learning or a recoverable small workload that fits the documented resource limits and can tolerate capacity interruptions. A requirement for guaranteed continuity needs a separate service assessment; Free Tier is not a reservation or an SLA. Your account's actual eligibility, live stock, final tax-inclusive bill and paid unit rates are <strong>Not obtained</strong>. The other unresolved items are the selected-image minimum boot size, account-specific A1 threshold and detailed reclamation/recovery procedure. Each missing input is named next to the calculation it blocks.</p>
<h2>Official sources and check date</h2>
<p>Checked 2026-11-13 07:11 UTC: <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier_topic-Always_Free_Resources.htm">Always Free Resources</a>, <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/Content/FreeTier/freetier.htm">Free Tier overview</a>, <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/faq/">Free Tier FAQ</a> and <a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/price-list/">OCI Price List</a>. This is a dated editorial check. Resource arithmetic and policy examples are ours; they are not measured account usage or a provider invoice.</p>
<p><a href="/">Home</a> · <a href="/pricing/">Pricing guide index</a> · <a href="/compare/">Compare published plans</a></p>'''
    return result

def publish_oracle(output,cfg):
    return publish_document(output,cfg,'/oracle-cloud-free-tier/','Oracle Cloud free tier: $0 starting cost, quotas and idle reclamation','Current official Always Free limits, resource-hour budgets, trial-expiry risks and an idle-reclamation checklist.',body(),CHECKED)
